\abstract(
Study the actual native producer from a tiny, inspectable example through the
retained original experiment and explicit boundary/work controls. Complete
editable C++ programs own every rendered native figure.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

A dense bucket is allocated for every integer value between the actual minimum
and maximum, including empty buckets. Each input is appended once; buckets are
scanned in increasing value order. The n+R cost includes R empty buckets, so a
huge sparse range is a poor input for this method. Range and value offsets are
widened before subtracting signed extremes, and the dense working range has an
explicit policy. Empty and singleton inputs retain the original no-bucket fast
path. Controlled integer fixtures suit this mechanism; no dataset is introduced.

$$ R=\max(a)-\min(a)+1,\qquad h(x)=x-\min(a),\qquad T(n,R)=O(n+R). $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table reads actual producing records. The native diagram names actual
captured values from that same run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pigeonhole_sort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/pigeonhole_sort.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = dm::algorithms::pigeonhole_sort_trace({3, 1, 3, 2});
    std::print("\n| actual input index | value | actual bucket | actual size after append |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.placements)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.input_index, r.value, r.hole,
                   r.count_after);

    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual allocated dense holes\n{}", t.run.holes));
    d.node("n1", {9, 0},
           std::format("Actual final occupancies\n{}", t.occupancies));
    d.node("n2", {18, 0}, std::format("Actual emitted values\n{}", t.run.sorted));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pigeonhole_sort_tiny.svg");
}
```
